.Dd October 6, 2026
.Dt SSH3-SERVER 8
.Os ssh3-c
.Sh NAME
.Nm ssh3-server
.Nd SSH3 server: user sessions and forwards over HTTP/3 (QUIC)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl l Ar addr:port
.Op Fl c Ar cert.pem
.Op Fl k Ar key.pem
.Op Fl A Ar alpn
.Op Fl d Ar dg_size
.Op Fl i Ar idle_ms
.Op Fl L Ar level
.Op Fl P Ar pwfile
.Op Fl K Ar authorized_keys
.Op Fl H Ar dir
.Op Fl -url-path Ar path
.Op Fl -enable-password-login
.Op Fl -oidc-issuer Ar url
.Op Fl -oidc-audience Ar id
.Op Fl -oidc-jwks-ttl Ar seconds
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl V
.Op Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
speaks the SSH3 transport of RFC 9220: one QUIC (UDP) listener carries
an HTTP/3 extended CONNECT to the
.Pa /ssh3-term
route (overridable with
.Fl -url-path ) ,
and every subsequent bidirectional stream is an SSH3 channel.
Shell and exec sessions, direct-tcp and direct-udp forwards, SFTP and
forward-agent bridges ride those channels; QUIC datagrams carry the
direct-udp control prefix.
The auth chain answers the CONNECT verdict: OIDC id_tokens
.Pq Fl -oidc-issuer ,
Bearer JWTs signed by
.Pq Fl K
authorized_keys keys (the conversation binds through the TLS
.Ev EXPORTER-SSH3
exporter), or Basic credentials against
.Pq Fl P
with the password login opted into.
Without any
.Fl K
the Bearer JWTs verify against the default identities chain of the
session user (see
.Sx FILES ) .
Every response, the refusals included, carries the
.Cm server
field with the protocol version the clients parse.
.Pp
Logs are one-liners on stderr (journald-friendly); the log file of
.Ev SSH3_LOG_FILE
is skipped when the process runs under systemd
.Pq Ev INVOCATION_ID .
.Pp
With no
.Fl l ,
.Nm
serves a systemd socket-activated listener; see
.Sx SOCKET ACTIVATION .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-enable-password-login"
.It Fl l Ar addr:port
UDP listen address:
.Li a.b.c.d:port
or the bracketed IPv6 form
.Li [v6]:port .
The
.Li [::]
bind serves both address families (IPV6_V6ONLY=0, the dual-stack
shape of the reference
.Fl -bind
default); a kernel that refuses the dual mode stops the daemon.
Port 0 picks an ephemeral one.  Optional under socket activation:
when LISTEN_FDS is in effect the passed sockets serve and an
.Fl l
argument is ignored (a warning is logged, nothing is bound).
.It Fl c Ar cert.pem
TLS certificate, PEM (required).
.It Fl k Ar key.pem
TLS private key, PEM (required).
.It Fl A Ar alpn
ALPN protocol name, default
.Ql h3 .
.It Fl d Ar dg_size
The max_datagram_frame_size transport parameter, default 1200.
.It Fl i Ar idle_ms
QUIC idle timeout in milliseconds, default 60000.
.It Fl L Ar level
Log level: a name
.Pf ( Ql debug ,
.Ql info ,
.Ql warn ,
.Ql error ,
.Ql all )
or a numeric s3 level.  An unknown name keeps the default.
.It Fl P Ar pwfile
Password file: lines of
.Li user:secret ;
the CONNECT passes only with matching Basic credentials AND the
password login opted into (the
.Fl -enable-password-login
flag or
.Ev SSH3_ENABLE_PASSWORD_LOGIN ,
the reference default is off).
.It Fl K Ar authorized_keys
Authorized_keys file, repeatable: the CONNECT passes only with a
Bearer JWT signed by one of the keys of any listed file, the files
walk in the given order.  A
.Cm %u
token in the path substitutes the session username (the
.Xr sshd 8
AuthorizedKeysFile shape); a path without it is one file for every
user.
Without any
.Fl K
the default chain of the session user serves.
.It Fl -url-path Ar path
The CONNECT route, default
.Pa /ssh3-term
(the reference
.Fl -url-path ) .
Must start with a slash; the query part of the request path carries
the username and does not affect the route.
.It Fl -enable-password-login
Opt into the Basic password method
.Pq the reference enablePasswordLogin .
.It Fl H Ar dir
SFTP jail directory override (the default is the user's home).
.It Fl -oidc-issuer Ar url
OIDC mode: the CONNECT passes only with a Bearer id_token of that
provider.  The discovery document and the first key set are fetched
once before the listener opens.
.It Fl -oidc-audience Ar id
The expected token audience (the client id).
.It Fl -oidc-jwks-ttl Ar seconds
Key-set lifetime of the OIDC provider, default 3600; the set rotates
in the background, an unknown kid schedules a refetch outside the
request path.
.It Fl v
Verbose logging (debug).
.It Fl V
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl h
Print the usage summary.
.It Fl 3
Accepted for compatibility with the interop harness; the SSH3 route
is the only mode of the daemon, the flag does nothing.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "SSH3_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN"
.It Ev SSH3_LOG_LEVEL
Same as
.Fl L .
.It Ev SSH3_LOG_FILE
Append-only log file; ignored under systemd (journald takes stderr).
.It Ev SSH3_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN
Graceful-shutdown window in seconds, default 5; 0 closes the
connections immediately, a negative or unparsable value falls back to
the default.
.It Ev SSH3_ENABLE_PASSWORD_LOGIN
With a truthy value
.Pf ( Li 1 ,
.Li true ,
.Li t ) ,
the Basic password method is opted in without the flag; the flag
overrides it (the reference env default for systemd
EnvironmentFile installs).
.It Ev SSH3C_PROTO
With
.Li 1 ,
machine-readable INTEROP-* markers go to stdout (the interop runner
protocol); production runs log one-liners instead.
.It Ev S3_OIDC_CA_FILE
Pins the HTTPS trust store of the OIDC discovery/JWKS fetches.
.It Ev SHELL
The program the session channels execute (default
.Pa /bin/sh ) .
.It Ev LISTEN_PID , Ev LISTEN_FDS
Read-only protocol of
.Xr sd_listen_fds 3 :
present together, the passed UDP sockets serve and
.Fl l
is not required; the markers are unset before any child is forked.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/ssh3/authorized_keys"
.It Pa ~/.ssh3/authorized_identities
First file of the default identities chain (the reference
DefaultIdentitiesFileNames), read for the session user when no
.Fl K
is given; missing files are tolerated.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
Second file of the default identities chain, the sshd shape.
.It Pa /etc/ssh3/cert.pem
TLS certificate (packaged default of
.Fl c ,
read by the service account).
.It Pa /etc/ssh3/key.pem
TLS private key (packaged default of
.Fl k ,
mode 0640 root:ssh3).
.It Pa /etc/ssh3/authorized_keys
Authorized keys (typical
.Fl K
target).
.El
.Sh SOCKET ACTIVATION
The packaged
.Pa ssh3-c-server.socket
binds UDP/443 and systemd passes the ready datagram socket to the
service:
.Nm
takes the fds at fd 3 upward, one or two serve.  A bare
.Li ListenDatagram=443
hands over ONE dual-stack IPv6 socket
.Pq BindIPv6Only=default ;
a
.Li 0.0.0.0:443
plus
.Li [::]:443
pair hands over TWO, each becomes its own listener and a connection
stays on the fd it arrived on.  Each fd is verified to be a datagram
socket of either family, set nonblocking and close-on-exec, the
LISTEN_* markers are unset and
.Xr bind 2
is never called; the IPv6 mode of the unit
.Pq IPV6_V6ONLY
is served as handed over and logged.
No capability
.Pq CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE
is needed by the service.
An fd of the wrong type or family, or more than two, stops the daemon
with an error instead of falling back to a second bind.
The listener address and port are owned by the socket unit
.Xr systemd.socket 5 .
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width SIGTERM
.It Dv SIGTERM Ns / Ns Dv SIGINT
Graceful shutdown: new connections are answered with
CONNECTION_CLOSE, the active conversations drain up to
.Ev SSH3_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN
seconds, then the leftovers close, the session children are killed
and the daemon exits 0.  A repeated signal closes everything at once.
.It Dv SIGPIPE
Ignored.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr systemd.socket 5 ,
.Xr sd_listen_fds 3 ,
.Xr sshd 8
